<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mardavij</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/935">935</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Mardavij ibn Ziyar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mardavij ibn Ziyar was a Gilite military leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziyarid-dynasty">Ziyarid dynasty</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Rising in the service of Daylamite commanders, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> and much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jibal">Jibal</a> around 930, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rayy">Rayy</a> and dreaming of restoring the Persian monarchy. He was murdered by his Turkish slave soldiers in 935, while the Buyid brothers, once his officers, built their own state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mardavij.jpg" alt="Mardavij" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MardavijCoinHistoryofIran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
